DEBUG: make the gaisler APBUART putc use the "drained" method (poll status bit1
TS = TX shift-register empty, one char fully transmitted before the next) instead
of bursting into the 8-deep TX FIFO via FIFOFULL (bit9).

On the a200t board the FIFO-burst path produces ~4x character duplication on the
wire (each char transmitted multiple times), while the drained method -- the same
one the boot stub and //bin/noelv_memtest use -- transmits cleanly. This makes
OpenSBI's own console output readable on hardware so its diagnostics (e.g. the
sbi_domain_init failure message) can actually be seen.

--- a/lib/utils/serial/gaisler-uart.c
+++ b/lib/utils/serial/gaisler-uart.c
@@ -43,7 +43,7 @@
 
 static void gaisler_uart_putc(char ch)
 {
-	while (get_reg(UART_REG_STATUS) & UART_STATUS_FIFOFULL)
+	while (!(get_reg(UART_REG_STATUS) & 0x2)) /* TS: TX shift empty (drained, no FIFO burst) */
 		;
 
 	set_reg(UART_REG_DATA, ch);
